  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="0becf7c1-9d31-5e06-ae2f-f04918e00147" activityNameId="9e50d499-b9be-5ff2-a25d-d4fa27b722b7" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electrolyzer production, 1MWe, PEM, Stack</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electrolyzer production, 1MWe, PEM, Stack
1 MW PEM electrolyzer stack based on Niklas Gerloff, Comparative Life-Cycle-Assessment analysis of three major water electrolysis technologies while applying various energy scenarios for a greener hydrogen production, Journal of Energy Storage, Volume 43, 2021, https://doi.org/10.1/j.est0.20.1. Lifetime of 45'000 hours per single stack, @ 8000 hours/year. Iridium mining process is NOT from ecoinvent. Produced amount of H2 over 20 years: 2,963,000 kg. In comparison to AEC electrolyzers, PEMEC electrolyzers are less mature. Furthermore, the PEMEC technology is commercially available and operates with a similar system efficiency as the AEC technology. However, the current density and the gas purity are higher with values in between 0.6â€“2.0â€¯A/cm2 and &gt; 99.99%, respectively. Besides this, the operating pressure (below 200â€¯bar) is significantly higher in comparison to AEC systems, while the operating temperature (50â€¯Â°C to 80â€¯Â°C) and the system energy (4.2â€“6.6â€¯kWh/m3H2) are similar to AEC systems. The PEMEC BoP and stack components data stem from BareiÃŸ et al. and correspond to a 1â€¯MW system. Moreover, some further BoP components like water purifier &amp; feed tank, buffer tank, and heat exchanger have been added, derived from a 300â€¯kW AEC system, under the assumption that the components are also suitable for a PEMEC system. The values have been scaled up from 300â€¯kW to 1â€¯MW. Stack lifetime: 5.5 years @ 8,000 hours per year. Replaced 3 times over systemÂ´s lifetime (20 years). For additional specifications, refer to Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023.

 UUID: f096f1ce-c80e-3dc4-89e2-d207aa45f336
